  {
   "id": 9,
   "type": "table",
   "title": "Hottest 12 vehicles right now",
   "description": "",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
    "uid": "quantara-pg"
   },
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 16,
    "y": 4,
    "w": 8,
    "h": 14
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {},
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "showHeader": true,
    "cellHeight": "sm"
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
      "uid": "quantara-pg"
     },
     "editorMode": "code",
     "format": "table",
     "rawQuery": true,
     "rawSql": "SELECT replace(k,'vss:','') AS vehicle, round(((payload->'vss'->>'Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Temperature.Average')::numeric),1) AS temp_c, (payload->'vss'->>'Vehicle.Speed')::float AS speed_kph, round(((payload->'vss'->>'Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Cooling.FlowRate')::numeric),2) AS coolant_flow, (payload->'edge'->>'cap')::float AS power_cap, round(extract(epoch from now())-ts) AS age_s FROM latest WHERE k LIKE 'vss:V%' ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 12",
     "refId": "A"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "What you are looking at",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 18,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 15
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "### How it works (left to right)\n1. **Vehicle simulator** (100 synthetic EVs) emits speed, battery temp, coolant flow, wheel speeds, suspension, steering, lamps, gear.\n2. **EDGE (on each vehicle)** applies a rulebook: *battery > 50 C* = cut power, *coolant stopped* = limp mode, bad CAN traffic = isolate. It decides in under a second, even with no network. Only what it cannot resolve is escalated.\n3. **Kafka** carries the data. **Validate** drops bad data and quarantines suspicious vehicles. **Enrich** converts to standard VSS signal names.\n4. **CLOUD** (only for escalations): ranks root causes (Bayesian), runs a **digital twin** what-if to pick a safe power cap, plans a **route** to a working charger, and (if enabled) asks **Gemini** for a second opinion.\n5. **OTA**: fixes are signed, range-checked, need owner consent, and roll out 5% -> 25% -> 100% with rollback. Everything is written to a hash-chained audit log.\n6. **This dashboard** reads the database that the ops sink fills. Data is synthetic only.\n\n### The 4 problem scenarios (open one, then inject it)\n| Scenario | Watch it here | Inject |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 Breakdown (heat, coolant dead) | [Dashboard 1](/d/quantara-s1) | `breakdown V000` |\n| 2 Ecosystem (grid / chargers down) | [Dashboard 2](/d/quantara-s2) | `grid_outage` |\n| 3 Degradation (km/kWh falling) | [Dashboard 3](/d/quantara-s3) | `degradation V000` |\n| 4 Cyber (attack on CAN / calibration) | [Dashboard 4](/d/quantara-s4) | `cyber_flood V000` |\n"
   }
  }
